QRDrop:
	When you insert a valid URL the app produces a QRcode and outputs it into outputPath. 
	outputPath is tmp/qrcodes/${uuidv4()}.png, and we can discover {uuidv4()}.png by trying to save the image of the QRcode (the suggested name is ${uuidv4()}.png)).
	Then we can put as input '; cp /flag.txt tmp.qrcodes/${uuidv4()}.png' and the QRcode image will be substituted by the flag.
	We can then print the flag by going to /qr/:filename and using as filename ${uuidv4()}.png. But we cannot see the image normally, since it is considered broken. 
	We can see the raw data by doing curl -i https://...


